### 4.1 Deployment (Louis runs or approves each)

1. `npx wrangler login`, then `npx wrangler d1 create blacklist`; put the `database_id` in `wrangler.jsonc`; `npm run db:migrate:remote`; `npx wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`; `npm run deploy`. The key's Console organisation needs web search enabled (it is unless an admin disabled it) and a monthly spend limit.
   - **Cost note.** Tool budgets and token costs are separate. The research loop enforces at most 10 searches and 12 fetches per run, across all its requests. Web search costs $10 per 1,000 searches, so at most $0.10 per run; web fetch has no per-call fee. Tokens are billed on every request: each continuation re-sends the whole conversation, including fetched page text (up to 8,000 tokens per fetch), so input tokens grow with each of the up to 5 requests. `max_uses` and `max_tokens` (24,000) are per-request ceilings, not spending caps. The Console spend limit is the only hard cap.
2. In Zero Trust, add Microsoft Entra ID as an identity provider (login method). This needs an Entra app registration with redirect URI `https://<team>.cloudflareaccess.com/cdn-cgi/access/callback`; group-based policies need admin consent.
3. Workers & Pages → blacklist → Access → Protect this Worker behind Access → All traffic. Policy: the SOC Entra group (or the Chorus email domain), with Entra ID as the only login method. Copy the team domain and the application AUD tag into `vars`, then `npm run deploy`.
4. First research run: set the cron to a daily time about 10 minutes ahead (keep it daily, because sub-hourly crons get only 30 s of CPU), deploy, confirm, restore `0 6 * * *` and deploy again.

